---
import { Copy, ExternalLink, Key, Plus, X, ChevronRight } from '@lucide/astro';
import DesignSection from '../DesignSection.astro';
import DoDont from '../DoDont.astro';
import DontExamples from '../DontExamples.astro';
import Stage from '../Stage.astro';
import TokenTable from '../TokenTable.vue';

const MOTION = [
  { name: '--time-fast', use: 'Hover colour.' },
  { name: '--time-base', use: "Disclosure chevron, the navigation drawer, a chart's first draw." },
  { name: '--time-slow', use: 'The sign-in spinner.' },
  { name: '--ease', use: 'Every transition. Starts fast, settles.' },
];

const ICONS = [
  { name: 'Plus', Icon: Plus },
  { name: 'Copy', Icon: Copy },
  { name: 'ExternalLink', Icon: ExternalLink },
  { name: 'X', Icon: X },
  { name: 'ChevronRight', Icon: ChevronRight },
  { name: 'Key', Icon: Key },
];
---

<DesignSection id="motion">
  <Fragment slot="definition"> Motion explains a change: something appeared, moved or finished. Nothing moves for atmosphere on working pages. </Fragment>
  <TokenTable client:load tokens={MOTION} caption="Motion tokens and their current values" />
  <div class="design-prose">
    <ul>
      <li>Only hover colour, a turning chevron, the sliding drawer, a small spinner and a chart's first draw move. Page content does not animate on load.</li>
      <li>With reduced motion requested, every transition and spinner stops and charts draw without animation.</li>
      <li>
        <b>Two named exceptions</b> are kept on purpose: the particle-track canvas (beside the Overview header and in the landing hero; one still frame under reduced motion) and the gateway diagram on the landing page (runs only on screen, never under reduced motion). Neither sits behind text a person needs to read.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</DesignSection>

<DesignSection id="icons">
  <Fragment slot="definition"> An icon repeats a label; it does not replace one. One set, Lucide, at one size. </Fragment>
  <div class="design-prose">
    <ul>
      <li>Icons are inline SVG, so they inherit text colour and need no network request or icon font.</li>
      <li>
        They come from the <code>@lucide/vue</code> and <code>@lucide/astro</code> packages, pinned in <code>package.json</code>; markup is never pasted by hand, so an icon can always be traced and updated.
      </li>
      <li>
        16px beside text, 20px in a large button. Lucide's default stroke; no per-icon weights or colours. <code>currentColor</code>, <code>aria-hidden</code> when decorative.
      </li>
      <li>An icon-only button has an accessible name. Status uses the status mark, not an icon.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <Stage label="Lucide at 16px, and in a large button at 20px" row>
    {
      ICONS.map(({ name, Icon }) => (
        <span class="af-st">
          <>
            <Icon class="af-icon" size={16} aria-hidden="true" />
            <code>{name}</code>
          </>
        </span>
      ))
    }
    <button type="button" class="btn" data-size="lg"><Plus size={20} aria-hidden="true" />New token</button>
  </Stage>
  <DoDont>
    <Fragment slot="do">
      <div class="design-stage__body is-row">
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-variant="outline"><Copy class="af-icon" size={16} aria-hidden="true" />Copy</button>
        <a href="#icons" class="design-link">Open CERN account settings <ExternalLink class="af-icon" size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></a>
        <button type="button" class="btn" data-variant="ghost" data-size="icon" aria-label="Dismiss"><X class="af-icon" size={16} aria-hidden="true" /></button>
      </div>
    </Fragment>
    <Fragment slot="do-note">pair an icon with its word. An icon-only button needs an accessible name.</Fragment>
    <DontExamples slot="dont" kind="glyphs" />
    <Fragment slot="dont-note">use text glyphs as icons. They change shape between fonts and platforms. An arrow is allowed only inside a sentence.</Fragment>
  </DoDont>
</DesignSection>
